# Flutter MVVM

Views render. ViewModels hold UI state. Repositories own data. Widgets never call Serverpod `Client` directly.

## Layers

- **View** — widgets only (layout, animation, navigation *calls*)
- **ViewModel** — `@riverpod` `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier` (`riverpod_generator`); expose immutable state + commands
- **Repository** — maps client protocol models → app domain models; caching
- **Use case** — only when logic is reused or too heavy for a ViewModel

**DI:** Riverpod in the widget tree (`ref.watch` / `ref.read`). **GetIt** only for long-lived singletons that non-widget code needs (Serverpod `Client`, repositories used by `GoRouter` redirects). Do not register ViewModels in GetIt.

After annotation changes: `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs` in that app.

## Folder layout (`lib/`)

```
core/di  core/theme  core/l10n  core/routing  core/widgets  core/errors
data/repositories  data/services
domain/models  domain/use_cases
features/<name>/views  features/<name>/view_models  features/<name>/providers
```

Shared widgets live in `core/widgets`, not copied per screen. Feature widgets that are not reused stay in the feature folder.

## Navigation

`MaterialApp.router` + **typed** `go_router` (`go_router_builder`: `@TypedGoRoute` / `GoRouteData`). Navigate with `const HomeRoute().go(context)`, not raw path strings. Auth `redirect` and role guards. No anonymous `Navigator.push` for app flows.

